From 7f98a0d2e7d7abcee2525e93080904634ef7b345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:47:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the Estuary ids of three changes apart, two entries
 read as one, the Spanish that was missing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three changes of 1.0 RC6 took the same Estuary ids. The ones of Dolby
Vision and HDR10+ keep theirs (GUIDialogSettingsBase computes its
mapping from them). The ids of the audio rows of the overview and of
whole-number multiples of the refresh rate, #32250 to #32253 and #32265
to #32266, are #32241 to #32246, next to #32240 of the same change; the
ids of the picture subtitles and of the Java notices, #32280 to #32288,
are #32290 to #32298. The entries are moved by their English text, so
that each keeps its own translations, and with them the references:
DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml, Variables.xml, the mapping in
GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp, BlurayJava.h, and the comments of the core
entries that name them.

Kodi reads a strings.po entry up to the next blank line
(CPODocument::GetNextEntry()). Two entries of the help of the black of
Low-Latency had no blank line after them, so that each was read as one
entry with the next and one of the two strings was lost: core #40981
(and its msgstr was missing) and Estuary #32277 in en_gb (msgstr
missing) and es_es. A blank line, and msgstr "" where it was missing.

The Spanish that was missing: every Hades string is in the four Estuary
files, en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx. The 32 Estuary entries of Dolby
Vision and HDR10+ were only in en_gb and es_es: they are in es_ar and
es_mx too, as in es_es with "video" for "vídeo", as the other Hades
strings of those two files have it. The four strings of the editions of
Matroska files (core #39805 to #39808) had none: Estuary #32286 to
#32289, read through CGUIUtils::GetHadesString() as the other Hades
strings are (the mapping of the setting, and the question itself in
MatroskaEditionChoice.cpp, which no longer needs two includes).

The core file's "empty strings" comment around the ids of the editions
and of whole-number multiples says the ids that are free.

system/hades made again by make-playerinfo.py: the moved ids, and what
the Dolby Vision and HDR10+ change added to Estuary's pages and that the
library did not have yet: the RPU measured because the output cannot
send HDR10, the values of "Content mapping sent", and the row of HDR10
adapted to the display.
